From adb0fa71b2c4dfc7fc05c7debadb146282341ab3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian <219239532+markd3ng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:54:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(expiration): support non-expiring pastes

Context: add the approved generic e=never and e=max expiration capability.\n\nExpected behavior: permanent pastes use null expiration metadata, omit KV TTLs, and use an explicit R2 permanent marker; MPU completion derives retention from create-stage metadata.\n\nAcceptance criteria: preserve timed parsing and clamping, return nullable expiration fields for permanent pastes, and keep cleanup/read paths null-aware.\n\nConstraints: upstream-owned generic code only; no downstream concepts.\n\nValidation: pnpm exec vitest run; pnpm typecheck; pnpm lint; pnpm build.\n\nDocs: doc/api.md, doc/curl.md.\n\nUpstream base: 0835cac4ab8f974035d31845f5c2b93b0c85b5c6\nPatch ID:      010-non-expiring-paste\nDependencies:  none\n\nRefs: https://github.com/Skyline-Gazer/pastebin-worker/issues/3\nhttps://github.com/Skyline-Gazer/pastebin-worker/issues/4
